-- 0349 — the audit's three slices arrive: cuisines, literary genres, comics & manga.
--
-- **The 2026-08-25 audit, owner: "fetch all three."** Three major parental
-- layers the tree measurably lacked: `hub:food_drink` held zero headings and
-- one lone cuisine-kind concept, in a dating app where food interest is a
-- first-order matching axis; fiction had no genres at all beside 292 academic
-- subjects, while `book` is a wire family and `author` a person kind; and the
-- ACG gap from the One Piece investigation — no manga or comics concept
-- anywhere, "Anime & manga" proposed by five grounded terms, shonen and
-- isekai below the TV-genre floor.
--
-- Same source, same posture, same twin-merge as `0346`. Wikidata (CC0):
-- cuisine (Q1778821, subclass walk >=25 — the national tier is instances of
-- a *subclass*, so direct P31 would miss Italy), literary genre (Q223393,
-- >=20), comic genre + manga genre (Q20087698/Q103112098, >=10 — manga
-- genres run fewer Wikipedias at the same renown). 293 headings:
-- 104 cuisines, 171 literary, 18 comics/manga with shonen and isekai among
-- them.
--
-- **Three new `medium:` layer nodes come first**, because `0348` established
-- that a genre never hangs from a bare hub — cuisines under
-- `hub:food_drink`, literary genres under `hub:ideas_learning`, comics &
-- manga under `hub:film_video` (the corpus's ACG interest is
-- screen-adjacent; the print home was considered and this is the deliberate
-- choice). "fantasy" and "science fiction" are absent by the tool's own
-- ambiguity guard — each label named more than one proposed concept — and
-- their screen-genre siblings from `0346` carry the concept-space.

